<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="8b10b0dc-c31a-5ac1-b889-669e3fab8552" activityNameId="06c978a2-7709-5b85-91c0-78764a81bfb6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, glider, for passenger car</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, glider, for passenger car
This dataset describes the shredding of the used glider of a passenger car. The entris are given per kg glider. The original data has been collected for the driver of a compact car with a glider weight of approximately 800 kg. Data is based on the e-waste shredding dataset which is based on literature. Infrastructure assumptions for the treatment facility are based on assumptions taken from weee. The output scrap and waste material quantities are derived from the respective glider dataset. The materialization of the glider is divided in 5 main fractions: scrap steel, scrap Aluminium, scrap Copper, scrap plastics and a shredding residue. These are the output waste flows of the process.The details concerning the materialization of the glider trated in this dataset are described in F. Habermacher  "Modeling material inventories and environmental impacts of electric passenger cars", Master Thesis, Department of Environmental Sciences, ETH Zurich, 2011.;
UUID: d0a5ab89-9134-36c5-a56a-bf1f83c204ae
The dataset takes as input the used glider and includes the treatment facility. This dataset returns the scrap fractions going to the specific recycling facilities and the emissions produced during the treatment process.
Location: Data from a European study, values used as global average data.
Technology: Modern Shredder facility with 2 shredder, 2 magnetic separation &amp; 2 Eddy-current separation steps.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 48000000000 kg
Sampling: own estimation 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d0a5ab89-9134-36c5-a56a-bf1f83c204ae.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
